Chameleon: copy at most the latest frame of a window per msc.

Xwayland copies every PresentPixmap as soon as it arrives, and Mesa's Vulkan
WSI presents asynchronously under Xwayland in mailbox mode, so a client
rendering at 1000 fps makes the server copy 1000 frames a second although
the compositor shows 60. A copy is cheap for a GPU blit, but with Chameleon a
client's own driver (turnip, panvk, ...) hands over buffers that Android's
driver cannot import, and each copy is a CPU copy.

Once a window has copied in the current msc, a present that would execute at
once is now held until the next msc, and a later one replaces it: the
replaced pixmap is idled immediately and its present completes as skipped,
as Xorg's present_scmd_pixmap() does. The first present of an msc still
executes at once, so a client that presents once per frame sees no change.

CHAMELEON_PRESENT_LATEST=0 restores Xwayland's own behaviour.

Written against xserver master of 2024-05-09 (just before xwayland 24.1.0).

--- a/hw/xwayland/xwayland-present.c
+++ b/hw/xwayland/xwayland-present.c
@@ -57,6 +57,30 @@
 
 static DevPrivateKeyRec xwl_present_window_private_key;
 
+/*
+ * Chameleon: showing a frame of a client that renders with its own driver
+ * costs a CPU copy in the server, so don't copy frames nobody will see. Once
+ * a window has copied in the current msc, a present that would execute at
+ * once is held until the next msc instead, and replaces the one held before
+ * it, which gets its pixmap back immediately and completes as skipped (as
+ * on Xorg). The first present of an msc still executes at once, so a client
+ * that presents once per frame sees no change.
+ * CHAMELEON_PRESENT_LATEST=0 turns this off.
+ */
+static Bool
+xwl_present_copy_latest(void)
+{
+    static int latest = -1;
+
+    if (latest < 0) {
+        const char *env = getenv("CHAMELEON_PRESENT_LATEST");
+
+        latest = !(env && strcmp(env, "0") == 0);
+    }
+
+    return latest;
+}
+
 static struct xwl_present_window *
 xwl_present_window_priv(WindowPtr window)
 {
